  {
    "label": "85e9a979-dd16-5177-b9bf-cda7e7a25733",
    "record": {
      "knowledge_point": {
        "db_id": 17592186083240,
        "id": "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a",
        "title": "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1t}{t+1},\\quad y=\\frac{1t^2}{t+4},\\quad t>0,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ as a function of $t.$\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{1\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t\\right)\\right)(t+1)-1t\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t+1\\right)\\right)}{(t+1)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{1\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t^2\\right)\\right)(t+4)-1t^2\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t+4\\right)\\right)}{(t+4)^2}\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{1(t+1)-1t(1)}{(t+1)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{2t(t+4)-1t^2(1)}{(t+4)^2}\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{1t+1-1t}{(t+1)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{2t^2+8t-1t^2}{(t+4)^2}\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{1}{(t+1)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{1t^2+8t}{(t+4)^2}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{\\frac{1t^2+8t}{(t+4)^2}}{\\frac{1}{(t+1)^2}}=\\frac{(1t^2+8t)(t+1)^2}{1(t+4)^2}.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
